1: /**
2:  * The registration flow that lets a new user create a Signal account without
3:  * supplying a phone number.
4:  *
5:  * The flow is an ordinary registration path with one difference: instead of an
6:  * SMS session it is unlocked by a one-time anti-spam purchase whose privacy
7:  * preserving proof of payment is exchanged for the account. Everything else -
8:  * preserving the issued login, optionally claiming a username, completing
9:  * registration - behaves the way it does for any other account.
10:  *
11:  * The flow owns state and decisions only. I/O lives in the dependencies handed
12:  * to it, so the flow can be rebuilt after a process recreation.
13:  */
